# React template

A great way to get up and running is by using the code from the [blocks page on Shadcn UI](https://ui.shadcn.com/blocks#blocks). All the blcoks have their code available to copy and paste into your project. Example `dashboard-01` has metric cards, charts, tables, and a sidebar navigation.

You can find other [components here](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components/). To add one, change directory into the `frontend` folder and run the command:

If you do not have `bun` installed, please see the section on [Mise-en-place](#mise-en-place) below.

```zsh
npx shadcn-ui add <component-name>
```

This template comes with a cli to handle managing the application through the terminal. To get started you can run:

```zsh
uv run {{ webapp_name }} --help

uv run {{ webapp_name }} install --help
uv run {{ webapp_name }} dev --help
uv run {{ webapp_name }} install --help
uv run {{ webapp_name }} start --help
uv run {{ webapp_name }} deploy --help
```

Some general points to note:

1. Don't use ccs files in the general case. [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/) covers the vast majority of use cases.
2. Use shadcn/ui components where possible. I will be implementing Nimbus themeing.
3. Page routing is being managed in `main.tsx`. Tanstack Router does want us to use a file based routing system, but I ended up prefering doing it manually.

